      // [src_mccartney_bb_eleanor, src_mccartney_bb_yesterday, src_mccartney_musicradar_emerick, src_mccartney_tapeop_emerick | 1965-1969 | session documentation + engineer] McCartney took the unfinished Eleanor Rigby to the other Beatles and Pete Shotton and took up their suggestions; on Yesterday he worked on the string score with Martin; Emerick says he dropped his elaborate Something bass line when Harrison asked for a simple one ('Paul complied') and that John liked his suggestion to slow Come Together. Against that, Emerick describes him swearing at Martin in the Ob-La-Di session. Mixed picture, so dual-edged and a moderate score.
      collaboration: [68, 0.62, "s", "D"],
